## OpenCode agent instructions

This project is driven through OpenCode. Keep these rules when delegating.

- **Skills live in `~/.config/opencode/skills/`** (user scope, populated by `install-skills.sh`) and
  in `{repo}/skills/` when the FlowForge clone is the workspace. Load a skill by reading its
  `SKILL.md` before writing any code.
- **Subagent-first delegation.** FlowForge marks its skills `metadata.opencode/autoinvoke: false`,
  so they are never auto-invoked. The orchestrator (`flowforge`) delegates each phase to its
  subagent — `forge-discovery`, `forge-arch`, `forge-plan`, `forge-dev`, `forge-verify`,
  `forge-memory` — instead of answering inline.
- **Skill loading order** for any task: (1) this `AGENTS.md`, (2) the phase skill named in its index,
  (3) the specialised skill under `skills/<skill>/<topic>/SKILL.md` when the trigger matches.
- **Checkpoints are blocking.** CKP-0 through CKP-4 are surfaced to the human; never advance past a
  red checkpoint on your own.
- **Read the `## Memory Signal`** a subagent returns and hand it to `forge-memory`; never call
  memory tools to persist your own summary.
- Do not edit `AGENTS.md` by hand — re-run `/fforge-init` so the managed block stays consistent.
